  file: shared/quarterly_notes.txt
    content signals: looks-like-password
    state: at rest (on disk) -> control: encrypt (SC-28) + restrict access (MP-2/AC-3)
    state: in transit (shared/copied across the network) -> control: TLS in transit (SC-8); DLP egress note
    state: in use (recently created/modified by a process) -> control: access enforcement (AC-3); minimize in memory

Honest reading recorded: the "in use" heuristic (recently modified) is a teaching
stand-in, not a detection; suggestions are starting points, not selections (the demo
doesn't know the classification tier); the structural finding is that every file is
in multiple states at once — single-state controls always leave gaps.

Worked case authored in-session: Aster Diagnostics control-selection matrix
(tier x at-rest/in-transit/in-use + scoping note + compliance mapping), DLP policy
sketch (tuned to tiers, staffed queue, 24h triage SLA), key-management decisions
(AES-256, FIPS-validated modules, KMS-held keys, annual rotation, separation of
duties). Differentiation from e-crypto-applied recorded: primitives there,
selection here. All company facts fictional.

